Z||000000||87ECO5||10-18-2001||02:03 PM||||I was looking to use Eibach lowering springs to stiffen up my suspension (I've got an '87 economy coupe with soft spring rates) but I don't want to lower the car.  Does Eibach or anyone else make springs that are as stiff as the lowering springs but maintain factory ride height?||||reg||5
Z||000001||mrfiero||10-18-2001||02:05 PM||||Nope.<P>Your only option is to install some stiffer factory springs.  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||87ECO5||10-18-2001||02:19 PM||||Do you have any GT springs for sale, Mike?||||reg||6
Z||000003||ray b||10-18-2001||02:22 PM||||stiffer tyres like 50 a/r will help tooo.<BR>or 17 inch with 35 a/r, looks better too.<BR>tyres are a big part of spring rates and eazyer to swap if you have 14" at least go to junkyards for cheap 15" alloy wheels and try 50 a/r tyres first.<P>------------------<BR>Question wonder and be wierd||||reg||1
Z||000004||mrfiero||10-18-2001||02:24 PM||||Actually, I do.  I have a pair of the stiffest front springs (don't know the code offhand) available from an '85 GT.....they should work just fine on your '87.  I don't, however, have a set of rears.  <P>Wait a minute......I do have an '85 SE junker.  Let me look at them and see how "stiff" they are.  <P>I'll let you know on the rears, but I definitley have the fronts (already off and ready to go).<P>LMK if you are interested.....I wouldn't want a whole lot for them.  Maybe $10 for the fronts + shipping and $10 for the rears + shipping (assuming I have stiffer ones than you already have).<P>LMK what you think. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||87ECO5||10-18-2001||02:26 PM||||I'm currently running 17" Konigs with 40 A/R Falkens.||||reg||1
